00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  it was important for china to excel at  the tokyo games  because they coincided with another  cause for celebration  the 100th anniversary of china's  communist party  having to see its athletes to excel in  these games  will validate the ccp's leadership as it  shows  china has the capability to win and to  excel  in the olympics and that will boost the  national confidence  and strengthen unity for china's leaders  olympic gold medals  represent an important projection of  power which is why  so much money is invested in finding the  very best  in china there's so many people that the  goal is to to weed through the many  people that are going through the system  and find the one that they think will  best represent the country  and is that more win at all costs than  another model is hard to say but  but they're there to win they're not  they're not there to come second that's  for sure  on the eve of the tokyo games the head  of china's olympic committee  said he wanted his country to win as  many gold medals as possible  that added to the pressure on china's  athletes and that same pressure  will doubtless be there when china hosts  the winter games  in just six months some of that pressure  was evident  when china's table tennis team lost to  japan  we lost the gold medal in the mixed  doubles match but our two teammates  lou shawn and xi singh tried their best  winning silver was not good enough  though and the duo  were attacked on chinese social media  with some bloggers  accusing them of failing the nation the  human story of somebody trying to do  their best to win a match gets caught up  in  historical or political events that have  nothing to do with the athletes  like japan china is tackling a  resurgence  in covid 19 along with its variants  winter games organizers also face other  challenges  corporate boycotts and protests  presumably there would be athletes  protest  uh against the china's human rights  issues  in relating to sensitive 